{%- comment -%}
  Renders one payment mark as inline monochrome SVG.

  Inline for the same reason as bf-icon: these sit in the footer, whose ink is
  red, black or cream depending on the theme, and inline SVG is the only form
  that inherits `currentColor`. An <img> would need three colour variants of six
  files; a CSS mask would cost six requests and lose the accessible name.

  Sources are the brand SVGs in the design repo (assets/icons/pg/), re-cropped to
  a tight viewBox so each mark can be height-normalised by CSS. The originals are
  drawn on square canvases with 30-60% empty padding, which would make them size
  unpredictably against each other.

  Each mark also carries its own optical height, set inline. They are
  deliberately not uniform: at one shared height the wide wordmarks (Visa, GPay,
  Paytm) read correctly, the enclosed marks (Mastercard, Amex) read small, and
  the portrait UPI arrow reads smallest of all. The three steps are a property of
  the artwork rather than a style choice, which is why they live here beside the
  geometry. Width follows from the viewBox; bf-base.css already resets svg to
  display:block.

  Accepts:
    mark - required, one of: visa, mastercard, amex, upi, gpay, paytm.
           An unrecognised value renders nothing.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-payment-mark', mark: 'visa' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign view_box = blank
  assign geometry = blank
  assign mark_label = blank
  assign mark_height = blank
-%}
